                                "sense_id": "6e4f3f3e-8fcd-34ca-ab7f-b4c96ad2ac17",
                                "text": "The katakana and the hiragana are syllabic forms of writing derived from Chinese characters, while the romaji are the letters used in writing most European languages.",
                                "translation": "片假名和平假名是衍生自汉字的音节书写形式，而罗马字则是用于书写许多欧洲语言的字母。"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "72eaf1eb-5df1-4300-acb8-a55fe3c7f28e",
                                "sense_id": "6e4f3f3e-8fcd-34ca-ab7f-b4c96ad2ac17",
                                "text": "For example, in Japanese advertisements sexy and my house often appear in romaji, making the underlying concepts of eroticism and private ownership more exotic.",
                                "translation": "例如，日本广告中的 sexy（性感）和 my house（自己的房子）经常使用罗马字书写，以分别使其潜藏的“色情”和“私人所有”的概念更加异域化。"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "37d53c48-be68-4a83-bf25-66a45d3370d5",
                                "sense_id": "6e4f3f3e-8fcd-34ca-ab7f-b4c96ad2ac17",
                                "text": "Today people ordinarily use kana-kanji conversion systems for inputting Japanese text. Because many of them can touch-type the romajis for the kanas, the O-code with kana-kanji conversion is more accessible."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
